# Used by builds whose context is the repository root. Today that is one image: services/console/Dockerfile (it copies
# console/ and services/console/). Every other Dockerfile is built with its own directory as the context and is not
# affected. Everything is excluded first, then what the console image copies is let back in, so a stray .env, a spike or
# a local build output can never end up in the build context (or in a layer).
*
!console
!services/console

# what must not travel even inside those two directories
**/node_modules
**/.svelte-kit
console/build
console/test-results
console/playwright-report
console/.vite
services/console/bin
services/console/web/dist/*
!services/console/web/dist/PLACEHOLDER
**/.env*
**/*.local
**/coverage.out

# named for clarity (the first line already excludes them)
.git
spikes
WHAT.txt
website/node_modules
